  {
    "id": "u00-l1",
    "title": "The four tones and the neutral tone",
    "summary": "Mandarin uses pitch to tell words apart. Learn the four tones and the light neutral tone.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "teach": {
          "title": "Four tones",
          "body": [
            "In Mandarin the same syllable means different things depending on the shape of its pitch. These shapes are called tones.",
            "Here are the four tones on ma. The pictures show each tone's shape, from low (bottom) to high (top). Tap each one to hear it."
          ],
          "contours": true,
          "items": [
            {
              "syllable": "ma1"
            },
            {
              "syllable": "ma2"
